{"info": {"author": null, "author_email": "Stanis\u0142aw Pitucha <viraptor@gmail.com>, ONEKEY <support@onekey.com>", "bugtrack_url": null, "classifiers": [], "description": "Arpy\n====\n\nThis library can be used to access **ar** files from python.\n\nIt supports both GNU and BSD formats and exposes the archived files using the standard python **file** interface.\n\nUsage\n=====\n\nStandard file usage:\n--------------------\n\nWith context managers:\n\n```python\nwith arpy.Archive('file.ar') as ar:\n    print(\"files: %s\" % ar.namelist())\n    with ar.open('content.txt') as f:\n        print(f.read())\n```\n\nVia headers for duplicate names:\n\n```python\nwith arpy.Archive('file.ar') as ar:\n    for header in ar.infolist():\n        print(\"file: %s\" % header.name)\n        with ar.open(header) as f:\n            print(f.read())\n```\n\nOr directly:\n\n```python\nar = arpy.Archive('file.ar'))\nar.read_all_headers()\n\n# check all available files\nar.archived_files.keys()\n\n# get the contents of the archived file\nar.archived_files[b'some_file'].read()\n```\n\nStream / pipe / ... usage:\n--------------------------\n\n```python\nar = arpy.Archive('file.ar'))\nfor f in ar:\n    print(\"got file name: %s\" % f.header.name)\n    print(\"with contents: %s\" % f.read())\n```\n\n\nContributions\n=============\n\nAll contributions welcome. Just make sure that:\n\n*  tests are provided\n*  all current platforms are passing (tox configuration is provided)\n*  coverage is close to 100% (currently only missing statements are those depending on python version being used)\n", "description_content_type": "text/markdown", "docs_url": null, "download_url": null, "downloads": {"last_day": -1, "last_month": -1, "last_week": -1}, "dynamic": ["License-File"], "home_page": null, "keywords": null, "license": null, "license_expression": "BSD-2-Clause", "license_files": ["LICENSE"], "maintainer": null, "maintainer_email": null, "name": "arpy", "package_url": "https://pypi.org/project/arpy/", "platform": null, "project_url": "https://pypi.org/project/arpy/", "project_urls": null, "provides_extra": null, "release_url": "https://pypi.org/project/arpy/2.4.0/", "requires_dist": null, "requires_python": ">=3.10", "summary": "Library for accessing 'ar' files", "version": "2.4.0", "yanked": false, "yanked_reason": null}, "releases": {"2.2.0": [{"comment_text": "", "core-metadata": false, "digests": {"blake2b_256": "b42d9a1fb66d3632a4646f52cf4d75cda1f14bf6fb74f1bf322236de347523e8", "md5": "0f98497e643f9135099d8c80e8d47a26", "sha256": "e07dfefc4cdf3d8b080e4b37e8c2b8360e7741b10faf6528f820b74999e0e6bc"}, "downloads": -1, "filename": "arpy-2.2.0.tar.gz", "has_sig": false, "md5_digest": "0f98497e643f9135099d8c80e8d47a26", "packagetype": "sdist", "python_version": "source", "requires_python": null, "size": 9251, "upload_time": "2021-01-13T10:59:16", "upload_time_iso_8601": "2021-01-13T10:59:16.491956Z", "url": "https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/b4/2d/9a1fb66d3632a4646f52cf4d75cda1f14bf6fb74f1bf322236de347523e8/arpy-2.2.0.tar.gz", "yanked": false, "yanked_reason": null}], "2.3.0": [{"comment_text": "", "core-metadata": false, "digests": {"blake2b_256": "d1d5a1985a4a645a1d66825e4cbb9fa7e8c5d10bf5b41fd32badb38b6b5e55ea", "md5": "dcd3e705626f90b8c51ec35ec68762a5", "sha256": "8302829a991cfcef2630b61e00f315db73164021cecbd7fb1fc18525f83f339c"}, "downloads": -1, "filename": "arpy-2.3.0.tar.gz", "has_sig": false, "md5_digest": "dcd3e705626f90b8c51ec35ec68762a5", "packagetype": "sdist", "python_version": "source", "requires_python": null, "size": 9572, "upload_time": "2022-06-11T05:07:00", "upload_time_iso_8601": "2022-06-11T05:07:00.319809Z", "url": "https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/d1/d5/a1985a4a645a1d66825e4cbb9fa7e8c5d10bf5b41fd32badb38b6b5e55ea/arpy-2.3.0.tar.gz", "yanked": false, "yanked_reason": null}], "2.4.0": [{"comment_text": null, "core-metadata": {"sha256": "5a69ddf151fff650dfbea267b8a36fbec0b8cdb54c8527822b546adf93b887c6"}, "digests": {"blake2b_2